  "description": "The top of the line Shift Plus i/O 9 is built upon a 140mm 4 bar link frame paired to a Rockshox Revelation 150mm travel fork. Its complimented with Shimano Di2 electronic shifting and an e8000 mtb specific mid motor drive system that's sure to satisfy the inner electronic geek in everyone. Shimano MTB specific e8000 drive unit with 250 watts of power, 70 Nm of torque, and 504 watt battery with a 4 hour recharge from flat form the power plant for the Shift i/O 9 which allows you glide uphill to do more of what you love...and that's fly right back down again. Simple light and convenient, Shimano XT 11 speed 1X keeps shifting clean and smooth while the all new Pivit internal dropper post with remote conveniently puts you in the right position at the right time. What goes down must go up, and with the power of i/O and e8000 you'll want to do it over, and over, and over again.\nShift Plus I/O X6 Aluminum frame for Shimano STePS E8000 motor, 140mm travel, tapered head tube 1-1/8\"-1.5\"\nRockshox Monarch RL 200mm rear shock, DebonAir, LL Tune, 430 lbs. lockout force\nRockshox Revelation RC 27.5\" Boost fork, 35mm stanchions, 15mm Stealth Maxle, Solo Air, 150mm travel, w/ hydraulic lockout\nShimano STePS E8000 drive unit / 250 Watts / 70Nm Torque, 500 w/h STePS & E8000 battery\nShimano XT Di2, 11-spd, Shadow Plus rear derailleur & shifter\nShimano XT 11-spd, 11-42T cassette\nShimano E8000 crankarms, forged, 38T chainring\nShimano SLX M7000 hydraulic disc brakes, Pads w/ fins, 180mm rotors\nTranzX Internal dropper post 100mm x 31.6mm\nNew Kenda Havoc 27.5\" x 2.6\" Folding tires",
